# Copy to .env.local and adjust.
#
# Every variable here is read when the server starts and then handed to the
# browser in the document, so the same image serves UAT and production with only
# these values changed: deployment promotes an artifact instead of rebuilding
# one. lib/runtime-config.ts is the single place that resolves them.
#
# The NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed spelling of each name is still accepted as a
# fallback, so images built before this existed keep working. Do not reach for
# it in new work: Next embeds NEXT_PUBLIC_* into the JavaScript it ships, which
# freezes the value at build time and welds the image to one environment.
#
# Nothing here is a secret either way — all of it reaches the browser.

# Base URL of the Go API the browser calls, including the /api/v1 prefix.
API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/api/v1

# The QRIS frame identity shown around the payment code. These must match what
# the gateway actually issues — the payment instructions tell the guest to verify
# the merchant name before entering a PIN, so a label that disagrees with the
# code defeats the check it invites. Re-verify whenever the merchant account
# changes. The values below were read off a code this gateway genuinely issued
# on 2026-08-10 (payload tags 59, 26->01 and 62->07).
QRIS_MERCHANT_NAME=Pupuk Kalteng
QRIS_MERCHANT_ID=936008580287697876
QRIS_TERMINAL_LABEL=659

# QRIS frame footer — the acquirer that issues the code and the printed layout
# version. Replace the acquirer code with the real one from the gateway team.
QRIS_ACQUIRER_CODE=93600008
QRIS_PRINT_VERSION=1.0-2024.11.13
